<body>

<div class="badge">PRODUCT OVERVIEW</div>
<h1 class="title">CRM</h1>
<h2 class="subtitle">A multi-client customer relationship platform built for healthcare organizations — clients, users and communication, unified in one workspace.</h2>

<table class="info">
  <tr><td class="k">Document</td><td>Product Overview — CRM</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">Prepared for</td><td>Internal / Stakeholder Presentation</td></tr>
</table>

<h1 class="section">Agenda</h1>
<ul>
  <li><b>Client Management</b> — Multi-tenant clients with access-level control</li>
  <li><b>Users &amp; Roles</b> — Granular permissions, per-user status</li>
  <li><b>Dashboard &amp; Reports</b> — Real-time visibility across the org</li>
  <li><b>Security</b> — Permission guards &amp; client-level access control</li>
</ul>

<h1 class="section">Why CRM</h1>
<p>One workspace instead of five disconnected tools.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Multiple clients, one login</b> — switch between organizations you have access to without juggling accounts.</li>
  <li><b>Consistent access control</b> — the same role &amp; permission model everywhere, not bolted on per-module.</li>
  <li><b>Built to scale with your team</b> — superadmins manage every client; client admins stay scoped to their own.</li>
</ul>

<hr class="page-break">

<h1 class="section">Client Management</h1>
<p>Every tenant is a Client — with its own users and data — created, viewed and edited from clean in-context popups, no page-hopping required.</p>
<table class="info">
  <tr><td class="k"><span class="status-active">Active</span></td><td>Full access</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k"><span class="status-inactive">Inactive</span></td><td>Disabled — no access</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k"><span class="status-suspended">Suspended</span></td><td>Locked — preview only</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Login itself respects this status — a suspended or disabled client is blocked at sign-in, not just hidden in the UI.</p>

<h1 class="section">Users, Roles &amp; Permissions</h1>
<ul>
  <li><b>Role-based access</b> — Every screen and action is gated by a named permission — view, create, edit, delete — assigned per role.</li>
  <li><b>Per-user status</b> — Active / Inactive toggle per employee, changed instantly from the user list.</li>
  <li><b>Cross-client access</b> — Superadmins can grant a user visibility into more than one client's data.</li>
</ul>

<hr class="page-break">

<h1 class="section">Dashboard &amp; Reports</h1>
<p>A live view of what matters — team activity and client-wide numbers — plus dedicated report screens for deeper analysis.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Team activity</li>
  <li>Client-level rollups</li>
  <li>Exportable reports</li>
</ul>

<h1 class="section">Security</h1>
<p>Access control, end to end.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Permission guards</b> on every page — a user without the right permission never sees the screen, not just the button.</li>
  <li><b>Client-status aware login</b> — Inactive or Suspended clients are blocked at sign-in with a clear message.</li>
  <li><b>Scoped data access</b> — users only see the client (or clients) they've been explicitly granted.</li>
</ul>

<h1 class="section">Technology</h1>
<table class="info">
  <tr><td class="k">Frontend</td><td>Next.js + React</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">UI</td><td>Bootstrap-based design system</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">Data</td><td>REST API integration</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">Auth</td><td>Token-based, client-scoped sessions</td></tr>
</table>

<h1 class="section">Why It Matters</h1>
<p>One CRM, every client you manage.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Faster onboarding</b> — New clients are up and running in minutes, not days.</li>
  <li><b>Modular by design</b> — Turn on only the modules a client needs.</li>
  <li><b>Built to grow</b> — Same platform scales from one client to a whole network.</li>
</ul>

<hr class="page-break">

<h1 class="section">Thank You</h1>
<p>CRM — one workspace for every client you manage.</p>

</body>
</html>
